  "note": "Complete individual Pitkäsilta bridge body: three shallow granite barrels, two broad piers with angular cutwaters, full mapped57m crossing and22.744m deck, granite spandrel courses and radial arch blocks, capped panel parapets and quiet geometric drop motifs, road, two tram tracks with four rails and crossing contact/suspension wires, six small suspended lamps, outer cycle/walk surfaces and short end bearings. Neighboring quays and bank-mounted wire supports remain native. Fixed21m visualization datum, approximate23m deck ends and23.25m center crown. Standard local water samples 19.048m; actual native water is separately measured in the renderer. The global urban field is biased above physical sea level; these fit controls and buried foundations are ordinary-photo approximations, not surveyed elevations."
